# Bind on every interface so teammates and coding harnesses (opencode, pi) reach vLLM directly.
#
# NOT the specific internal IP, even though that is what you usually want to hear: start_all.py's
# readiness poll (line ~186), check_vlm.py's default, and the Flask proxy's VLM_SERVE_UPSTREAM_HOST
# all dial 127.0.0.1. Binding a single NIC silently removes the loopback path all three depend on,
# and start_all.py's failure mode is to stop each model it cannot reach — the whole bring-up dies.
# 0.0.0.0 is a superset: it covers the internal IP *and* loopback.
#
# Restricting *who* may reach the port is a firewall/security-group rule — that is the layer that
# actually enforces it. site.env's VLLM_API_KEY is the second gate — serve_vlm.py passes it as
# --api-key itself, so there is deliberately no API_KEY line here to drift from it.
HOST=0.0.0.0

# 나머지 knob(DTYPE, GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION, MAX_MODEL_LEN, MAX_NUM_SEQS,
# TENSOR_PARALLEL_SIZE)은 모델마다 값이 달라서 여기 두지 않는다 - 전부
# config/models/<slug>.env 에 명시하고, 빠졌을 때의 기본값은 serve_vlm.py 가 쥔다.
# 같은 기본값을 두 곳에 적으면 어느 쪽이 이기는지가 로드 순서에 달리게 된다.

# MODEL_ID 는 반드시 이 루트 아래여야 한다 (오프라인 검증 - 런처가 항상 확인한다).
ALLOWED_MODEL_ROOT=${MODEL_ROOT}
